  "kinds": {
    "_comment": "Instinct kinds: who the Pokemon deals with. ambient = background life with no counterpart (hanging, resting, drinking, howling...); player = towards or for a player (flee, follow, heal, steal, harass, retaliate...); pokemon = against other Pokemon and mobs (hunts, packs, formations, breeding, rivalry); world = changes blocks or items (tunnels, snow, fire, nests, crops); spawn = creates Pokemon (hordes, raids); trait = nature/ability modifiers. enabled false leaves every entry of that kind unattached. intensity (0-2) multiplies the global intensity for that kind's chances and cooldowns. maxActivePerPlayer above 0 caps how many WILD Pokemon may run a non-free instinct of that kind at once around one player (0 = no cap). An entry can change its kind with \"kind\" in its params.",
    "ambient": {
      "enabled": true,
      "intensity": 1.0,
      "maxActivePerPlayer": 0,
      "hang": {
        "_comment": "Natural cocoons (normal Cobblemon spawns, not from broken leaves) hanging from trees. Each area of areaSize x areaSize blocks fills up to targetPerArea hanging cocoons (each new one hangs with fillChance), may grow up to maxPerArea (extraChance, only without lag) and never beyond; maxPerPlayer caps the dimension at that many per player in it (0 = no cap). The decision is stored on the cocoon, so reloading a chunk does not change it. A cocoon that finds no tree maxSeekFailures times stops looking. naturalHorde lets a natural hanging cocoon bring a few more, only up to its area's target. Cocoons from broken leaves always hang and count. natural false = only cocoons from broken leaves hang. scaleWithHeadroom (0.12.0) lets the performance governor relax these limits while the server has room: an ambient scale s from 0 to 1 moves targetPerArea, maxPerArea, maxPerPlayer and fillChance towards their relaxed* values (and cocoon_horde towards its relaxed* group). s = h * max(c, h), where h is the server headroom (1 up to globals.headroomFullMspt smoothed ms per tick, 0 from headroomZeroMspt or with lag) and c the player factor (1 with fewPlayers or fewer online, 0 with manyPlayers or more). s = 0 is exactly the 0.10/0.11 behaviour. Only new decisions use the current s; a cocoon that already decided to hang keeps its place up to the relaxed limits.",
        "natural": true,
        "areaSize": 32,
        "targetPerArea": 2,
        "maxPerArea": 4,
        "maxPerPlayer": 24,
        "fillChance": 0.6,
        "extraChance": 0.15,
        "maxSeekFailures": 2,
        "naturalHorde": true,
        "scaleWithHeadroom": true,
        "relaxedTargetPerArea": 7,
        "relaxedMaxPerArea": 10,
        "relaxedMaxPerPlayer": 64,
        "relaxedFillChance": 0.9,
        "fewPlayers": 4,
        "manyPlayers": 30
      }
    },
    "player": {
      "enabled": true,
      "intensity": 1.0,
      "maxActivePerPlayer": 0
    },
    "pokemon": {
      "enabled": true,
      "intensity": 1.0,
      "maxActivePerPlayer": 0
