    {
      "id": "steal_item",
      "enabled": true,
      "_comment": "Steals items from nearby players, then flees and eats them if they are edible. 'targets' fixes WHAT can be stolen and replaces 'preference' when it is not empty: categories food, precious, tools, weapons, armor, blocks, any; a tag such as #c:gems; or an item id such as minecraft:diamond (a bare 'diamond' matches any namespace). Anything that does not match is never stolen, and with nothing to steal the thief does not even charge. Worn armor is never taken. Thefts from players are paced per PLAYER, not per thief (globals theftLevel, theftMaxPerDay, theftMinGapMinutes, theftChance and the theft*Multiplier keys): any number of thieves nearby steal as often as one; 'useTheftBudget': false brings back the old per-thief cooldown for this entry. 'hotbarOnly' (default globals.theftHotbarOnly) limits thefts to the 9 hotbar slots. Example: [\"precious\", \"tools\"]. Empty list = old behaviour (preference only orders, and anything can be taken). What the thief carries is dropped back when it is hurt (dropWhenHurt), dies, is captured, starts a Pokemon battle or its chunk reloads; only food it eats is lost.",
      "species": [
        "nickit",
        "thievul"
      ],
      "priority": 2,
      "params": {
        "preference": "food",
        "targets": [],
        "dropWhenHurt": true,
        "triggerRange": 12.0,
        "speed": 1.45,
        "fleeSpeed": 1.6,
        "damage": 2.0,
        "stealCount": 1,
        "fleeTicks": 140,
        "eatTicks": 40,
        "consume": true,
        "stealFromCreative": true,
        "cooldownTicks": 600
      }
    },
