        ],
        "dropWhenHurt": false,
        "triggerRange": 10.0,
        "speed": 1.3,
        "fleeSpeed": 1.6,
        "damage": 0.0,
        "stealCount": 1,
        "fleeTicks": 240,
        "consume": false,
        "stealFromCreative": false,
        "cooldownTicks": 1200,
        "tease": true,
        "teaseDistance": 8.0,
        "teaseKeepAway": 4.0,
        "scaredKeepAway": 14.0,
        "holdMaxTicks": 6000,
        "ransomFood": [
          "#cobblemon:berries",
          "minecraft:apple",
          "minecraft:melon_slice",
          "minecraft:sweet_berries",
          "minecraft:glow_berries",
          "minecraft:honey_bottle",
          "minecraft:cookie"
        ],
        "ransomChance": 0.45,
        "ransomRange": 8.0,
        "inspectTicks": 30
      },
      "_comment": "DISABLED BY DEFAULT. Mischievous thief: takes one precious item or tool, backs off only a little (teaseDistance) and keeps watching you. If you hit it, it flees with the item and keeps farther away (scaredKeepAway). To get it back, throw it any food: ransomFood (its favorites) always works, any other food has ransomChance of being taken; then it looks at the item and drops it at its feet. After holdMaxTicks it gets bored and drops it. Dying, capture or a battle always return the item. Placed before the older Aipom/Ambipom entry on purpose: the first enabled entry wins, so enabling this one replaces that entry for Aipom and Ambipom."
    },
    {
      "id": "steal_item",
      "enabled": true,
      "_comment": "Monkeys with a taste for shiny things: gems and gold first, then other metals, then food.",
