        "launchUp": 0.85,
        "xpMaxLevel": 50,
        "knockbackMax": 1.6,
        "launchUpMax": 1.2,
        "burstDamage": 1.0,
        "burstDamageMax": 3.0,
        "slowFall": false,
        "dizzy": true,
        "levitateTicks": 0,
        "stunTicks": 60,
        "nauseaTicks": 100,
        "selfTeleport": false,
        "escapeTeleportMin": 12.0,
        "escapeTeleportMax": 20.0,
        "healFraction": 0.25,
        "playersOnly": false,
        "wildOnly": true,
        "chargeEnabled": false,
        "chargeHits": 6,
        "armorPerHit": 2.0,
        "maxChargeArmor": 10.0,
        "chargeBurstDamage": 4.0,
        "recoveryTicks": 100,
        "hitWindowTicks": 200,
        "vortexTicks": 60,
        "pulseIntervalTicks": 4,
        "criticalHealthFraction": 0.15,
        "pullStrength": 0.12,
        "maxPull": 0.25,
        "maxTargets": 8,
        "particlesPerPulse": 12,
        "spiralArms": 3,
        "radiansPerTick": 0.15,
        "spiralHeight": 3,
        "maxBurstDamage": 12,
        "maxKnockback": 1.5,
        "baseLaunch": 0.25,
        "launchPerLevel": 0.002,
        "maxLaunch": 0.7,
        "levelDivisor": 50,
        "maxLevel": 100,
        "maxLevelScale": 2
      },
      "_comment": "Psyduck headache: each real hit makes it worse (headacheHits within hitWindowTicks); then it bursts, launching nearby players and Pokemon into the air and leaving them dizzy (stunTicks). It only teleports away after a heavy hit (heavyHitFraction of its max HP), at low health (fleeHealth) or below escapeBelowLevel, and never before bursting. Experimental charge/vortex mode remains opt-in. The burst grows with the experience LEVEL of each player it hits: knockback, launch height and magic damage (never lethal, ignores armor) go from the base values at level 0 to knockbackMax, launchUpMax and burstDamageMax at xpMaxLevel (0 turns the scaling off). slowFall false means no slow-falling cushion, so the landing hurts (less with Feather Falling); set it true for the old soft landing."
    },
